# Helix layout

Adapt at the shell — do not invent per-page chrome.

| Breakpoint | Chrome | Edge gutter |
|------------|--------|-------------|
| `< lg` | Top header + bottom tabs | Content / header use `px-3` |
| `lg+` | Framed sidebar + unframed main slot | Outer `p-2` + `gap-2` (equal all sides) |

- Main pane on `lg+`: no glass/border card — work area is the content column.
- Page column: `max-w-6xl` + `px-3` + `py-4` (same on every route).
- Desktop header title sits inside the same `max-w-6xl` column as page content.
- Use `h-dvh` for full-height frames (not `h-screen`).
- Login stays full-bleed cinematic — no sidebar.
- Tables: horizontal scroll on small screens; widen inside the content column on desktop.
